Replace server-name-only client pools with owner-scoped managers and independently managed upstream lifecycles. Preserve unchanged clients, bound connection startup, and handle subprocess context-manager ownership, cancellation, and cleanup. Never reuse credentials or sessions across users. Acceptance: same upstream names under two users use separate credentials/connections; partial startup, disconnect and cancellation tests pass without leaked tasks/processes.
